      "username": "joneirik",
      "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/j/ecb155/{size}.png",
      "created_at": "2019-03-05T00:55:01.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>tldr: the topic.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>One thing that has annoyed me to no end in the core box, is that the invader board is about 1x2cm too large to fit inside the box without having to fold it, and been wondering why it wasn't made slightly smaller ? But when I opened Branch and Claw and got another foldable board (events), I thought it was a lot of wasted table space and box space compared to what it could have been ?</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>After trying to re-pack and organize the entire game + expansion in various boxes last couple of days, I thought it would be much more practical to have the \"Invader board\" + \"Event board\" printed on a playmat (basically a large mouse pad for those not familiar with them from card games like MtG or Codex etc). So I could just roll it up and stuff it into a side pocket or something.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Is this something you (Eric/GtG) would be interested in doing and put up on the store? Or is this something I could do myself? (scan the boards, and order a custom printed playmat online), Alternatively, something to throw in on the Jagged Earth Kickstarter ? (Backed the full thing btw)</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Outside of that, thanks for great game, we've been playing it a lot locally, and is currently the favorite game of a few of us. Been spending last two days buying more sleeves (for branch and claw), deck boxes to fit all the cards, and a new toolbox/briefcase to fit everything inside. Since the original box and the plastic inserts became completely useless with sleeves and expansion added. Since I tend to carry it around so often.</p>",
